      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/5/5013",
      "text": [
        ": \"لاَ يُجَرَّدُ فِي حَدٍّ وَ لاَ يُشْبَحُ يَعْنِي يُمَدُّ\" وَ قَالَ \"يُضْرَبُ اَلزَّانِي عَلَى اَلْحَالِ اَلَّتِي يُوجَدُ عَلَيْهَا، إِنْ وُجِدَ عُرْيَاناً ضُرِبَ عُرْيَاناً وَ إِنْ وُجِدَ وَ عَلَيْهِ ثِيَابُهُ ضُرِبَ وَ عَلَيْهِ ثِيَابُهُ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5013 - Talhah ibn Zayd narrated from Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) from his father, Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as), that he said:\n\"A person should not be stripped of their clothing nor stretched out (meaning tied or extended) for any legal punishment.\"\nImam (as) also said: \"The adulterer should be beaten in the state in which they are found; if they are found unclothed, they are beaten while unclothed, and if they are found clothed, they are beaten while clothed.\""
        ]
      }
    },
